{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Introduction to JAX Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Setup and Data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We will train a 3-layer MLP on MNIST using JAX and Optax. 784 inputs, two hidden layers of 256 and 128 neurons, 10 output classes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import jax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import jax.numpy as jnp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from jax import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import optax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def get_mnist_data():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    from sklearn.datasets import fetch_openml"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mnist = fetch_openml('mnist_784', version=1, as_frame=False, parser='auto')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    X = mnist.data.astype('float32') / 255.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y = mnist.target.astype('int')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    X_train, X_test = X[:60000], X[60000:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y_train, y_test = y[:60000], y[60000:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Initialize Parameters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "No class. Just a function that returns a pytree:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def init_params(key):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    k1, k2, k3 = random.split(key, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scale1 = jnp.sqrt(2.0 / 784)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scale2 = jnp.sqrt(2.0 / 256)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scale3 = jnp.sqrt(2.0 / 128)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        'layer1': {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            'w': scale1 * random.normal(k1, (784, 256)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            'b': jnp.zeros(256),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        'layer2': {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            'w': scale2 * random.normal(k2, (256, 128)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            'b': jnp.zeros(128),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        'layer3': {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            'w': scale3 * random.normal(k3, (128, 10)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            'b': jnp.zeros(10),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "He-initialization, done manually. Three PRNG keys split from one seed. Every weight is an immutable array in a nested dict."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Forward Pass"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def forward(params, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = jnp.dot(x, params['layer1']['w']) + params['layer1']['b']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = jax.nn.relu(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = jnp.dot(x, params['layer2']['w']) + params['layer2']['b']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = jax.nn.relu(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = jnp.dot(x, params['layer3']['w']) + params['layer3']['b']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def loss_fn(params, x, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    logits = forward(params, x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    one_hot = jax.nn.one_hot(y, 10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.log_softmax(logits) * one_hot, axis=-1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Pure functions. Params in, prediction out. No `self`, no stored state. `loss_fn` computes cross-entropy from scratch -- softmax, log, negative mean."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: JIT-Compiled Training Step"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@jax.jit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_step(params, opt_state, x, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params, x, y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return params, opt_state, loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@jax.jit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def accuracy(params, x, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    logits = forward(params, x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    preds = jnp.argmax(logits, axis=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return jnp.mean(preds == y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`jax.value_and_grad` returns both the loss value and the gradients in one pass. The `@jax.jit` decorator compiles both functions to XLA. After the first call, each training step runs without touching Python."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Training Loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate=1e-3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test = get_mnist_data()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test = jnp.array(X_train), jnp.array(X_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y_train, y_test = jnp.array(y_train), jnp.array(y_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "key = random.PRNGKey(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "params = init_params(key)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "opt_state = optimizer.init(params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "batch_size = 128"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "n_epochs = 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for epoch in range(n_epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    key, subkey = random.split(key)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    perm = random.permutation(subkey, len(X_train))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    X_shuffled = X_train[perm]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y_shuffled = y_train[perm]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    epoch_loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_batches = len(X_train) // batch_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n_batches):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        start = i * batch_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        xb = X_shuffled[start:start + batch_size]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        yb = y_shuffled[start:start + batch_size]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params, opt_state, loss = train_step(params, opt_state, xb, yb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        epoch_loss += loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    train_acc = accuracy(params, X_train[:5000], y_train[:5000])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_acc = accuracy(params, X_test, y_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Epoch {epoch + 1:2d} | Loss: {epoch_loss / n_batches:.4f} | \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          f\"Train Acc: {train_acc:.4f} | Test Acc: {test_acc:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "10 epochs. ~97% test accuracy. The first epoch is slow (JIT compilation). Epochs 2-10 are fast."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Notice what is missing: no `.zero_grad()`, no `.backward()`, no `.step()`. The entire update is one composed function call. Gradients are computed, transformed by Adam, and applied to parameters -- all inside `train_step`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add dropout to the MLP. In JAX, dropout requires a PRNG key -- thread a key through the forward pass and split it for each dropout layer. Compare test accuracy with and without.\n\n2. Use `jax.vmap` to compute per-example gradients for a batch of 32 MNIST images. Compute the gradient norm for each example. Which examples have the largest gradients, and why?\n\n3. Replace the manual forward function with a generic `mlp_forward(params, x)` that works for any number of layers. Use `jax.tree.leaves` to determine the depth automatically.\n\n4. Benchmark the training step with and without `@jax.jit`. Time 100 steps of each. How large is the speedup on your hardware? What is the compilation overhead on the first call?\n\n5. Implement gradient clipping by composing `optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(1e-3))`. Train with and without clipping. Plot the gradient norm over training to see the effect."
      ]
    }
  ],
